WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:05.530
I activate the spell card 
Polymerization from my hand!

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:06.460
What?

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:11.320
I fuse together Edge Imp 
Sabres and Fluffal Bear.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.800
Devil's claws and beast's fangs!

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.600
Become one and show your new power and look!

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.870
Fusion Summon!

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:29.760
Appear, the hair-raising beast 
that slashes everything!

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.360
Frightfur Bear!

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:47.700
Master, I'll show you what 
I'm like when I'm serious!

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:57.240
Implementing mass into Solid 
Vision has created Action Duels.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:05.110
In duels where the field, monsters and duelists 
become one, the people are caught in a frenzy of excitement!

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.350
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.130
You!  The strongest card 
isn't about winning or losing

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:31.540
You!  At full speed  On the game

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.280
Swinging ma ma ma mind

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:44.850
The soul's pendulum  Ultimate confusion

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.050
Impulse  Got it got it

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:52.260
Tough battles  Real revolution

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:03.070
Everybody goin'  Break through the walls!

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:09.940
Infinite future  Get rid of indecision!

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.880
Make it Make it  Be courageous (Break it now)

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:17.280
Step ahead!  Take a step (Do it now)

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:27.560
The fun is only getting started!  
So everyone's a Believer!!

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.900
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:41.000
Innocent Toy
Frightfur Bear

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:10.980
He used the spell card Polymerization to 
combine his two monsters into a stronger monster.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.220
This is...

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.240
Fusion Summon!

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:17.980
I heard that LDS has recently 
started teaching it.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:21.820
Is he a LDS student?

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:25.550
He was going to enroll at 
LDS, but he decided not to.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.550
Let's battle, Master!

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:32.530
First, I'll make you get off 
your fleet-footed hippo.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:36.890
Frightfur Bear attacks Hip Hippo!

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.220
Yuya!

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.910
Yuya!

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:03.510
Frightfur Bear's effect activates.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:07.550
Frightfur Bear can equip 
the monster it destroys.

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:08.930
What?

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:17.970
Hippo!

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:22.980
I equip the destroyed Hip 
Hippo on Frightfur Bear!

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:34.710
Frightfur Bear gains attack points 
equal to the monster it equips.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.600
It grew in size!

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.690
3000 attack points!

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:46.660
Frightfur Bear now has more attack 
points than Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:51.300
So if he takes an attack, 
Odd-Eyes will be destroyed?

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:55.420
The more monsters it destroys, 
the stronger it gets.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:59.310
Frightfur Bear is terrifying.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:06.090
Oh my!  Master, what happened 
to your confidence?

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:10.980
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:14.090
My turn!  I draw!

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:23.470
Frightfur Bear is a powerful enemy, but 
Odd-Eyes and I have friends that will fight alongside us!

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:27.460
I activate Performapal Sword Fish's effect!

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:37.240
Once per turn, this card lowers your 
monster's attack points by 600!

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:43.290
Frightfur Bear has fewer 
attack points than Odd-Eyes!

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:45.590
He can now destroy it in battle!

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:46.790
Let's battle!

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:51.060
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon 
attacks Frightfur Bear!

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.710
I activate the trap Punch-in-the-Box!

00:05:54.710 --> 00:06:02.060
When I'm attacked, this card sends one of 
your non-attacking monsters to the graveyard.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:09.050
Your attacking monster loses attack points 
equal to that monster's attack or defense points.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.640
And your attack is negated!

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:12.890
I won't let you do that!

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.040
I activate Timegazer 
Magician's Pendulum Effect!

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:24.260
Once per turn, when you use a trap card on my Pendulum 
Monster, that trap's activation and effect are negated!

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.870
Inverse Gear Width!

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:34.930
He used Timegazer Magician's Pendulum Effect!

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:39.910
He reversed time so that 
the trap never activated.

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:41.510
Incredible!

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:44.840
But what will you do about the second card?

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.530
I activate a second trap card!

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:51.780
It's Punch-in-the-Box again!

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:54.750
What?  He has another copy of that trap?

00:06:55.060 --> 00:07:00.930
He expected Timegazer Magician's Pendulum 
Effect, so he already set another Punch-in-the-Box!

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:06.040
Timegazer Magician's Pendulum Effect 
can only be used once per turn.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.170
He can't stop this trap!

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:13.310
I send Skeeter Skimmer to the graveyard!

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:27.330
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon's attack is negated, and it 
loses attack points equal to Skeeter Skimmer's defense points.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:32.800
Odd-Eyes loses 1600 attack points.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:40.130
C'mon, Master.  Don't look so mean.

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:43.910
I switch Sword Fish to defense position.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:51.240
Oh my.  Master, you're playing passively.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:54.000
Can it be that you're out of options?

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.910
If that's true, I'm disappointed.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:59.780
I thought our duel would be more fun.

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:00.890
How boring.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:04.840
I set one card and end my turn.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:11.640
Sword Fish's effect lowered Frightfur Bear's 
attack points, but they now return to normal.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:16.350
Yuya...

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:20.980
My turn!  I draw!

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.860
This might end the duel.

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:29.920
I activate the spell card 
Toy Parade from my hand!

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:38.090
This turn, my Toy monster can attack 
for every monster it has equipped.

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:39.380
What?

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:42.070
This is bad!  Very bad!

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:43.690
Bad?

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:48.400
Frightfur Bear only has Hip Hippo equipped.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:53.330
That means it can only attack 
once, so it's the same as normal.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:55.330
I get it!  That's not true!

00:08:55.330 --> 00:09:04.400
The moment Frightfur Bear destroys and equips my 
monster, Toy Parade's effect will let Frightfur Bear attack again.

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:06.890
Well done, Master!

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:08.460
You understand!

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:10.530
I see.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:16.720
If Frightfur Bear destroys a monster and 
equips that monster, it can attack again.

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.750
And if it equips the next one...

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:21.810
It can attack for a third time.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:26.380
Yuya will have no monsters on 
his field, so that means...

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:30.220
I'll attack you directly and win!

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:35.240
This is the power of a Fusion Monster!

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.860
Yuya is going to lose?

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:39.060
It'll be fine.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:42.730
This isn't enough to make Yuya quit.

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:47.550
I'll start off by crushing 
your ace monster Odd-Eyes.

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:55.910
Due to Toy Parade's effect, Frightfur Bear gains attack points 
every time it destroys a monster, and it also can keep attacking.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:10:00.000
If this combo comes to fruition, 
I'll definitely lose.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.580
I can only stop it by preventing 
Odd-Eyes's destruction.

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:06.090
In order to do that...

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:11.460
I won't let you.  Frightfur Bear!

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:15.130
Let's go, Odd-Eyes!

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:22.890
It's mine!

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:29.110
What?

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:37.550
Incredible!

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:39.110
He's so agile!

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:41.510
Which school did he attend?

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:48.220
In order to get an Action Card, you 
need to use your monsters skilfully.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:52.770
I made the right decision to destroy your 
Hippo first so that you couldn't ride it.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:55.730
You even planned for that?

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:58.670
It's time for the battle 
we've been waiting for!

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.710
Frightfur Bear attacks 
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:08.000
I won't let you!

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:11.080
I activate the trap card Command Performance!

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:16.560
When there's a Performapal on my field, 
your monster switches to defense position!

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:21.240
I should play an Action Card!

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:24.660
I activate the Action Spell Candy Coat!

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:38.930
Due to this card's effect, your spells and 
traps can't affect my monster this turn.

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:41.380
And it can't be destroyed in battle!

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:45.110
Too bad, Master.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:49.600
If you were able to grab this card, you 
could've prevented Odd-Eyes's destruction.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.060
Damn!

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:54.400
Frightfur Bear, resume your attack!

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:05.950
Odd-Eyes!

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.510
Yuya!

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:21.390
My Odd-Eyes was...

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.400
Master, are you okay?

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:26.860
It looks like you took heavy damage.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:29.270
This match has been decided.

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:33.730
Yuya is frustrated by how 
this duel turned out.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.830
That's not all.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:40.180
Odd-Eyes was proof that Yuya 
took a courageous step forward.

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:44.080
It was the symbol of Yuya's 
creation: Pendulum Summon.

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:47.420
Yuya's heart took damage.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:51.380
Don't lose, Yuya!

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:55.110
Yuya...

00:12:55.510 --> 00:13:02.130
I guess I'll leave my depressed 
Master alone and take his Odd-Eyes.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:07.060
Frightfur Bear, equip the destroyed 
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon.

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:21.640
Where did it go?

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:23.150
What's wrong, Yuya?

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:28.530
Dad!  I lost my pendulum!

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:31.240
I see.  That is a problem.

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:36.490
But that's no reason to 
hang your head in shame.

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:38.740
Lift your head up.

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:42.670
When you want to cry during tough 
times, lift your head and laugh.

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:45.510
If you do, you can move forward.

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:46.620
But...

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.550
Just do it.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.950
There it is!

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:01.720
See?  Your dad was right.

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:06.210
Laugh when you want to cry.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:08.260
Right, Dad?

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.640
That's right.

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:22.440
If my heart is in defense position, 
I can't have a fun duel.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:27.020
My motto is to have a cheerful 
and fun entertainment duel.

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:33.060
I can't entertain people 
if I don't enjoy my duel!

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:41.640
What?

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:44.620
This is the Extra Deck.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:48.840
But my deck doesn't have any 
cards in the Extra Deck.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:51.950
What's going on?

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.420
Why can't I find Odd-Eyes?

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:14.530
The destroyed Odd-Eyes 
isn't in the graveyard.

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:19.550
Odd-Eyes is in the Extra Deck!

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:24.440
When did it go there?

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:28.710
Inside the Extra Deck?

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:36.800
How interesting, Master!

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:42.350
Destroyed Pendulum Monsters go to the 
Extra Deck instead of the graveyard!

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:44.350
I've never experienced this before!

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:46.930
Pendulum Monsters are the best!

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:50.440
If it's not in the graveyard, 
Frightfur Bear can't equip it.

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:54.700
My attack is over.  I end my turn!

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:58.300
Master, entertain me next turn!

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:00.940
Yeah!  I'll show you my turn!

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:03.780
The fun is only getting started!

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:07.250
Good.  I've gathered all the actors.

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:11.860
Watch, everyone!

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:19.060
Scale 1 Stargazer Magician and Scale 8 
Timegazer Magician are set on the stage!

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:24.930
That means I can summon monsters 
between Levels 2 and 7 simultaneously!

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:31.170
Swing, my soul's pendulum!

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:34.140
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:35.770
Pendulum Summon!

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:42.350
First, I will introduce you 
to a new Pendulum Monster!

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:46.660
Level 2 Performapal Cheermole!

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:53.960
And one more!

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:02.490
Resurrect with radiance, 
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:18.180
Pendulum Monsters can also be 
summoned from the Extra Deck!

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.310
It gives me shivers!

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:25.460
Even if it's destroyed, it goes to the Extra Deck 
instead of the graveyard, so it can resurrect over and over.

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:28.880
This is Pendulum Monsters' additional power!

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:32.600
That's incredible, Yuya!  
Pendulum Monsters are hot!

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:34.930
I'm burning up!  My blood is burning!

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:42.510
Watch what the supporting roles 
do to support the leading actor!

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:51.880
Once per turn, Performapal Sword Fish lowers 
your monster's attack points by 600!

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:56.080
Everyone, it's time for a simple math quiz.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:58.080
What's 3000 minus 600?

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:00.060
2400!

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:03.480
Odd-Eyes has 2500 attack points.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:06.030
It can destroy Frightfur Bear!

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:07.770
Exactly.

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:14.230
I have the trap card Punch-in-the-Box 
that you negated.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:20.330
But even if I activate it, Timegazer 
Magician's effect will negate it again.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:23.880
So I can't prevent Frightfur 
Bear's destruction.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:25.530
Correct!

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:30.580
But even if you destroy Frightfur Bear, 
I'll only take 100 points of damage.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.960
That's not good enough to defeat me!

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:35.690
Are you sure?

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:41.100
I activate Performapal Cheermole's effect!

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:48.710
Please focus your attention 
on the cute Cheermole's cheer!

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:57.030
So cute!

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:07.760
Once per turn, Cheermole powers up an attack 
point-changing effect by 1000 points!

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:11.780
Cheermole powers up Sword Fish's 
effect, and I activate it!

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:25.130
Sword Fish's effect lowered its attack 
points by 1600 instead of 600!

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:28.130
That gives me shivers!

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:41.830
When Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon battles a Level 
5-or-above monster, its effect doubles the damage you take!

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:45.260
That means...

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:48.580
Everyone, all together now!

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.700
Battle!

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:56.230
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon 
attacks Frightfur Bear!

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:58.740
Go, Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:02.880
Burn everything you see with 
your different-colored eyes!

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:06.080
Spiral Strike Burst!

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:23.480
He did it!

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:25.280
Yuya won!

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:26.530
How wonderful!

00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:47.830
Do you remember your promise?

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:51.230
Since I won, you're not my apprentice-

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:52.830
That was fun!

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:56.680
Dueling you was really fun, Yuya!

00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:59.970
Why are you calling me 
Yuya instead of Master?

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:05.280
If you won't let me be your apprentice, 
then I'm going to be your friend, Yuya!

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:08.030
If we're friends, I can call you Yuya.

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:09.530
That's not your choice-

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:12.680
I see.  You two have become friends.

00:21:12.680 --> 00:21:14.830
A student's friend is also a student.

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.880
So why don't you enroll 
in my You Show School?

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:22.830
Sure!  This place seems 
much more fun than LDS!

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:28.280
All right!  I'll bring an 
enrollment form immediately!

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:34.270
But if you're not an LDS student, 
where did you learn to Fusion Summon?

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:39.750
Where I used to live, it was normal 
for everyone to do Fusion Summoning.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:43.480
Normal?  Where?  In another country?

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:48.690
Don't sweat the details 
because we're friends now.

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:50.430
What's up with that?

00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:53.680
Besides, I didn't accept you as a friend yet.

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:56.630
We're buddies, Yuya.

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:00.730
Stop deciding things on your own!

00:22:00.730 --> 00:22:03.330
Since I'm joining this school, 
we can play even more!

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:05.380
Let me see your duels, Yuya!

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:07.230
Stop deciding things on your own!

00:22:07.230 --> 00:22:10.630
I will never accept!

00:22:13.460 --> 00:22:18.940
Catch the dream dancing in my heart
Release my falling tears

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:28.420
I'll step out on to my first field
To meet my miracle  Fabulous One Step

00:22:35.310 --> 00:22:40.430
I realized that strength can't be given

00:22:40.690 --> 00:22:45.670
It's something I have to grab myself

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:51.110
In that case, I have to keep moving
I can't stay still

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:56.370
Even if walls and headwinds block my way

00:22:56.570 --> 00:23:01.970
I'll draw my trump card called 
"courage" to take a step forward

00:23:01.970 --> 00:23:06.390
I believe in my story of victory

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:12.360
Everyone during battle is My Way
Duelists are being tested

00:23:12.360 --> 00:23:17.770
When times are tough, that's when you 
Smile, Jump, Fight & Step Up!

00:23:17.770 --> 00:23:23.100
Your smile is your Energy
Kick away your feelings of running away

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:32.440
Jump into the new field
Shiny One Step that leads to the future

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:40.660
One step... Just one step is fine
That's your Big Chance!!

00:23:45.280 --> 00:23:50.730
You coward!  I won't let you do 
whatever you want to defeat Yuya!

00:23:50.730 --> 00:23:55.330
Yuzu Hiiragi, you're courageous 
for challenging me to a duel.

00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:58.680
Who are you to suddenly barge in?

00:23:58.680 --> 00:24:03.380
I don't know who you are, but 
Neo Sawatari will pummel you!

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.930
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V:
Revolution of Wrath
Dark Rebellion Xyz Dragon

00:24:09.930 --> 00:24:12.530
The fun is only getting started!
